A||||16||86SE||Anyones Temp guage ever stick?||||8||
Z||000000||86SE||02-03-2000||11:10 PM||||On start-up my temp guage used to always peg to the right and stick!!  The person who owned the fiero be 4 me smacked the top of the pod with a lighter and put small crackes in the top of it.<P>Then I found out its all in the wireing!!<P>Wired it up the right way and now works like a charm!!<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||2birds||02-04-2000||11:04 PM||||Mine started doing this about three or four years ago.  It only does it when the interior is really hot, and I'm guilty of whacking the top of my dash with my hand.  One whack usually does the trick.  I think I saw something in the online service guide about the meter getting full battery voltage at startup, but I don't understand the relationship to the air temp in the car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||daved||02-04-2000||11:18 PM||||Two, this is a common problem we all have. The factory wiring is wrong, causing the needle to swing up on startup, sticking to the gooey dust gasket.  I rewired mine, but it isn't easy. There was a thread about this a couple of months ago.||||reg||1
Z||000003||86SE||02-05-2000||12:06 AM||||How long did it take to wire yours??  It took me about 10 min, I thought it was pretty easy.<P>If I remember right, you just cut and cap 1 wire and take the other half and splice into 2 others....||||reg||1
Z||000004||Luperman||02-05-2000||09:40 AM||||hey 86SE can you tell me exactly how you did it or email pleaaaaase because it is very erritating  and I hate banging on my dash .<BR>                               thanx||||reg||5
