Z||000007||GT Bastard||02-05-2000||07:38 PM||||Oh yeah, and the heat from the flames melted the whole interior to my body.  Very painful. I screamed.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||02-05-2000||09:13 PM||||Not to get too off topic here(thats monkeys job  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">), but I'm not really convinced the "guage peg on startup" is a mistake. The Fiero is the only car I've ever seen do it in person, but the Fiero is the only GM I've ever ridden/driven.  <BR>Ferris Bheulers day off was on today, and when Ferris starts Cameron's dads Ferrarri(sp?), all the guages peg while the starter is enguaged. Granted, maybe it was not a real one, but they still did the peg thing. Maybe even "exotic" cars do it too. I like that idea  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 02-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||daved||02-05-2000||11:09 PM||||56, it IS a mistake. If you put your key in the "test bulb" position, you will notice that the Hi Temp. bulb does not come on, while the gauge is pinned to the top! The factory got the wiring reversed, its a simple as that.||||reg||1
Z||000010||DRH||02-06-2000||03:28 AM||||Mistake is probably not the right word. That would imply it was not designed that way. Since EVERY Fiero built over 5 years does this it would seem to be intentional. Maybe they WERE trying to copy some other sports car.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I think "poor design" would be a better description. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 02-06-2000).]||||reg||12
Z||000011||Formula||02-06-2000||10:48 AM||||My Formula doesn't do that.  I wonder if someone fixed it before.  <P>does anyone have an 88 V6 that does this?<P>and does your battery gauge do it too?||||reg||1
Z||000012||fiero56||02-06-2000||11:29 AM||||My '88 v-6 temp guage pegs. It never sticks though. I'm not sure about the the voltmeter or others, I would have to check.||||reg||1
Z||000013||DRH||02-07-2000||02:01 AM||||My 88 Formula does pegs but has not stuck in the 8000 miles I have had it.<P>The volt meter does not peg.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||DJRice||02-07-2000||09:42 AM||||You dont have to rewire the gauges to fix the problem.  That is to say, There are ways to prevent the gauge from getting stuck, but your temp light wont flash on startup.  <P>I bought a pack of little black rubber anti-skid feet from RadioShack and put one of those inside the gauge.  With the black metal cover on the gauge assembly, you cant even tell they are there, and the gauge does not swing high enough to get stuck.  <P>No wire cutting/splicing required!||||reg||1
Z||000015||theogre||02-07-2000||07:49 PM||||You can unplug the gauge wire from the steering column switch in about 10 minutes. It's the only light green wire on it as I recall. You have to take the plug off the switch, then you use a little screw driver to release the terminal. put a bit of tape over the loose terminal.<P>That won't fix the idiot light, but it will stop the gauge peg. You don't have to rip appart the whole dash to fix it.<P>To get to the switch take off the trim pannel then loosen all 4 of the bolts that hold the bracket of the steering column to the bottom of the dash. remove the right bolt, or is it a nut, closest the seat if you need more room. The rest you should only have to loosen. you need a 7mm nut driver, a 9/16 socket, and a small screw driver.<P>This problem was left uncorrected because niether GM or NHTSA/USDOT see it as a safety problem. It costs money to make even small changes to a vehicle in production.<P>It is posible to repair the harness with no cutting at all. The terminal used in the ignition switch is used in other places. (The rear defog and trunk latch to name 2) Use a spare terminal, or get one at the parts store, stuffed in the location vacated by the one you just took out. Then connect it to the dark green wire on the back right of the dash. You can either make the connection by tacking it to the dash connector, or by using a speed tap.<P>((this is one of those things I have to put in Tunnel 6.))<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 02-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||GREENDANO||02-09-2000||06:18 PM||||Here's the link to end all questions...<BR>----&gt; <A HREF="http://www.tir.com/~jaski/tempgauge/tempgauge.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tir.com/~jaski/tempgauge/tempgauge.htm</A> <P>Dan-O||||reg||1
